ng, Lohit, Subansiri, Manas) in the east.","distinctive_features":"Acts as an impenetrable climatic divide protecting the Indian subcontinent from arctic Siberian winds while intercepting southwest monsoon air masses; major global biodiversity hotspot.","economic_significance":"Vast hydroelectric generation potential, perennial freshwater reservoir, international alpine and pilgrimage tourism, temperate horticulture (apple, walnut, saffron), and rich reserves of timber and medicinal flora.","states_covered":["Jammu and Kashmir","Ladakh","Himachal Pradesh","Uttarakhand","Sikkim","Arunachal Pradesh","Nagaland","Manipur","Mizoram","Tripura","Meghalaya","Assam (hill tracts)","West Bengal (Darjeeling)"]}},
