to 2,000 meters in central sections.","economic_significance":"Known as the 'Granary of India'; supports over 40% of the national population through intensive multi-cropping agriculture (wheat, rice, sugarcane, jute), supported by high water tables and dense transport-industrial corridors.","states_covered":["Punjab","Haryana","Delhi","Uttar Pradesh","Bihar","West Bengal","Assam","Northern Rajasthan"]}},
