,[72.7,24.13],[72.61,24.15],[72.44,24.37],[72.48,24.49],[72.62,24.64],[72.66,24.73],[72.61,24.8],[72.75,25],[72.86,25.05],[73.02,25.21],[73,25.23],[73,25.23],[73.16,25.44],[73.15,25.57],[73.29,25.77],[73.26,25.98],[73.49,26.11],[73.48,26.2],[73.6,26.34],[73.57,26.36],[73.57,26.38],[73.73,26.56],[73.68,26.7],[73.91,26.81],[74.1,26.97],[74.17,27.08],[74.09,27.17],[74.16,27.35],[74.3,27.47],[74.3,27.47],[74.35,27.44],[74.6,27.67],[74.63,27.76],[74.79,27.94],[74.83,28.12],[74.95,28.23],[74.95,28.34],[75,28.38],[75,28.38]]]]},"properties":{"class_key":"peninsular_plateau","name":"Peninsular Plateau","color":"#ffcda2","sub_divisions":"Central Highlands (Malwa, Bundelkhand, Baghelkhand, Chota Nagpur), Deccan Plateau (Maharashtra/Deccan Trap, Karnataka Plateau, Telangana Plateau), and Northeastern Extension (Shillong/Meghalaya Plateau and Karbi Anglong). Flanked by the Western Ghats and Eastern Ghats.","geological_origin":"Oldest, most stable tectonic shield of India; a relict part of Gondwanaland composed of crystalline Archaean granites, gneisses, Dharwar schists, and extensive Cretaceous Deccan basaltic volcanic flood sheets.","relief_and_topography":"Inverted triangular tableland gently tilting from west to east; elevation ranges between 600 and 900 m; characterized by flat-topped mesas, buttes, rounded hills (monadnocks), fault scarps, and structural rift grabens (Narmada-Tapi troughs).","drainage_and_rivers":"West-flowing rift valley drainage: Narmada, Tapi, Mahi, Sabarmati. East-flowing peninsular drainage discharging into the Bay of Bengal: Mahanadi, Godavari, Krishna, Kaveri, Penner, Subarnarekha, Wainganga, Bhima, Tungabhadra, Indravati.","distinctive_features":"Surrounded by asymmetric margins—the continuous, precipitous Western Ghats (Sahyadris) and the fragmented, heavily dissected Eastern Ghats; features senile, mature river valleys with low grading.","economic_significance":"Mineral powerhouse of India (rich deposits of coal, high-grade iron ore, bauxite, mica, manganese, and limestone); vast fertile black soil tracts for cotton and oilseeds; premier coffee, tea, and spice plantations on the Ghat summits.","states_covered":["Madhya Pradesh","Chhattisgarh","Jharkhand","Odisha","Maharashtra","Karnataka","Telangana","Andhra Pradesh","Tamil Nadu","Kerala","Eastern Rajasthan","Southern Uttar Pradesh","Meghalaya"]}},
