ans, exposed rocky pediments, and dry salt depressions (playas/dhands/ranns).","drainage_and_rivers":"Internal, ephemeral endorheic drainage; the Luni is the solitary integrated river system reaching the Rann of Kutch during monsoon; dotted with saline playa basins (Sambhar, Didwana, Pachpadra).","distinctive_features":"Extreme aridity with annual rainfall below 150 mm; high diurnal temperature ranges, low vegetative cover, and shifting dunes (*dhrians*); underlain by extensive fossil wood formations (Akal Wood Fossil Park) reflecting paleoclimatic shifts.","economic_significance":"Global hub for solar and wind renewable energy harnessing; valuable mineral resources (gypsum, marble, lignite, bentonite, petroleum reserves in the Barmer-Sanchore basin); thriving irrigated oasis agriculture along the Indira Gandhi Canal.","states_covered":["Western Rajasthan","Southwestern Punjab","Southern Haryana","Northern Gujarat (Kutch fringe)"]}},
